Z||000016||Nashco||12-13-2001||07:02 PM||||I lived in Snohomish (close to Seattle) almost my whole life, and I can honestly say that the list is pretty much true.  Those who think some aren't true just haven't spent enough time in enough other major cities! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I think I fit myself into about 35 of those 38 easily...<P>Another strange thing about life in Seattle is commuting to work on a boat(ferry).  Lots of people live around other areas in the Puget Sound and commute on a ferry every morning.  One of few places in the U.S. that this is common occurence from what I've seen so far.<P>Another trend I miss, but that is not necessarily just a northwestern thing is cutting down your own Christmas tree.  Down here in 'bama pretty much everybody buys their's in parking lots... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Patrick's Dad||12-14-2001||09:49 AM||||&lt;quote&gt;18. Understand what people mean when they say "pop." (Translation: soda)&lt;/quote&gt;<P>You mean "tonic?"<P>&lt;quote&gt;27. Know how to pronounce: Sequim, Puyallup, Rainier, and Issaquah.&lt;/quote&gt;<P>How about Chicatawbut, Cochato, or Wolomolopoag? My wife and I pronounce "Samoset" differently, and we grew up about 15 miles away from each other.<P>&lt;quote&gt;33. Are amazed at an accurate weather forecast.&lt;/quote&gt;<P>You mean there is such a thing? For more than five minutes?||||reg||1
Z||000018||Formula88||12-14-2001||10:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>Another trend I miss, but that is not necessarily just a northwestern thing is cutting down your own Christmas tree.  Down here in 'bama pretty much everybody buys their's in parking lots...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, but that's cuz if you went to cut down your own tree in 'bama, some hayseed would shoot you for cutting down a tree on his property!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Personally, I prefer fake trees.  Let's celebrate life and joy and happiness, by killing a tree!  I don't get it.  But that's also because I grew up with a fake tree.  (1) tree my entire childhood, so that became the family Christmas tree.  Lots of sentimental value attached.  Guess that makes a difference.||||reg||1
